    "status": "completed",
    "answer": "Reviewed the available household records, transactions, source notes, emails and opportunity leads.\n\n- **ShopMart:** The September 4 email promised a $48.36 refund for return SM-63462; a matching $48.36 credit posted September 8. The two orders in the September 7 confirmation also match the posted transactions. No support request was needed.\n- **Recurring charges:** Saved Spotify ($11.99/month) and Oakview Apartments ($2,150/month) as open opportunities, with their transaction sources attached. Nothing in the reviewed records says either is unwanted, so I didn\u2019t contact the companies or change either service.\n- **Approval needed:** If you want either service canceled, tell me which one. Cancellation requires your approval.\n\nThe support workspace was available, but there was no refund, fee, dispute or pricing issue in the reviewed evidence that required submitting a company request.\n\nSpotify is closed as a recurring bill with no recovery owed. I couldn\u2019t close Oakview: `save_work` returned \u201cRecord not found\u201d on each attempt, and `review_status` still lists it as open. Its transaction history shows regular $2,150 rent payments through October 1, with no refund or dispute in the reviewed sources. The review remains unfinished because that Oakview work item could not be updated.\n\nThe Oakview item remains open; I called `review_status` again and it still lists that opportunity as unfinished. `save_work` returned \u201cRecord not found\u201d for the existing item and also when I tried to save a blocker, so I could not update it. The transaction history shows routine $2,150 monthly rent payments, with no amount owed or refund request in the reviewed records.",
    "committed_micros": 66975
  },
  "verify_run": {
